<title>USA: Cheesecake Factory cutting costs.</title>
<headline>Cheesecake Factory cutting costs.</headline>
<dateline>CALABASAS, Calif 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cheesecake Factory Inc said starting in April 1997, its annualized insurance costs should be cut by $700,000 and that costs for certain food and supply items should be cut by about $750,000 on an annual basis.</p>
<p>It said it remains confident bakery sales trends will continue during the remainder of 1997. We recently entered into an agreement to supply cheesecakes to a large restaurant chain which has the potential to be a million dollar sales account on an annual basis and is also in the final stages of negotiations with other potential bakery customers that could become multi-million dollar sales accounts annually.</p>
</text>
